{"id":1066,"date":"2020-11-19T18:49:55","date_gmt":"2020-11-20T02:49:55","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1066"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:40:43","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:40:43","slug":"build-the-trailer-bot","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/build-the-trailer-bot\/","title":{"rendered":"Build the Trailer Bot"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22161b969a1\" name=\"6a22161b969a1\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>The head<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Attach four short L-frames to one blueboard. When you&#8217;re finished, flip it upside down.<\/li>\n<li>Attach five long L-frames to another blueboard, with the long ends in the air.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1067&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1068&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22161b96ac8\" name=\"6a22161b96ac8\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Attach the battery box<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Use one more long L-frame to attach the battery box to the long L-frame at the back of the blueboard. You can position the battery box wherever you want, but make sure the short end of the L-frame is sticking up and over the top of the battery box.<\/li>\n<li>Use two short standoffs to make one stacked standoff.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt a 4-hole metal frame to the top of the battery box&#8217;s long L-frame with a nylon nut.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt the stacked standoff onto the end of the 4-hole metal frame.<\/li>\n<li>Attach your blueboard with the short L-frames to your blueboard with the long L-frames.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1069&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1070&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1071&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22161b96b2d\" name=\"6a22161b96b2d\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Attach the DC motors and wheels<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Bolt the motor casings to the tops of the long L-frames.<\/li>\n<li>Attach the wheels to the motors with black screws. The wheels will stay attached without the black screws if you don&#8217;t have them.<\/li>\n<li>Flip your Trailer Bot over so the wheels are on the ground.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1072&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1073&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22161b96b89\" name=\"6a22161b96b89\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Attach the Smart Inventor Board<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Bolt two long standoffs to the Smart Inventor Board. Pay attention to their placement!<\/li>\n<li>Attach the Smart Inventor Board to the bottom of the Trailer Bot. The Smart Inventor Board should be touching the ground, or at least be very close to it.<\/li>\n<li>Attach two long standoffs to the top of the Trailer Bot.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1074&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1075&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1076&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22161b96be0\" name=\"6a22161b96be0\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Build the trailer<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Bolt two short L-frames to the edges of one blueboard.<\/li>\n<li>Use two 4-hole metal frames to attach this blueboard with another blueboard. When you&#8217;re finished, flip it upside down.<\/li>\n<li>Make eight sets of stacked standoffs with short standoffs and attach them to the two blueboards. Pay attention to their placement!<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1077&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1078&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22161b96c3f\" name=\"6a22161b96c3f\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Build the trailer's rails<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Bolt two 10-hole metal frames to each other to make one long metal frame. The edges should be overlapping. Repeat so you have two long metal frames!<\/li>\n<li>Bolt the long metal frames to the tops of the stacked standoffs. You&#8217;ll also need to bolt two 7-hole metal frames to the tops of the standoffs so you have a metal frame rectangle. Next, add two long standoffs to the front and bolt a 7-hole metal frame to that.<\/li>\n<li>Attach two horn brackets to the short L-frames underneath the blueboards.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt one of the standoffs on the bottom of the trailer to the L-frame on the battery box.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1082&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1083&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1084&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1085&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22161b96c9d\" name=\"6a22161b96c9d\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Wire the Trailer Bot<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Before you start wiring your Trailer Bot, make sure the Smart Inventor Board is facing you.<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The motor on your right is M1.<\/li>\n<li>The motor on your left is M2.<\/li>\n<li>Attach the motors to their respective spots on the Smart Inventor Board (M1, M2, M3, and M4 are all marked).<\/li>\n<li>Make sure that the red wires are the in the negative position (facing the inside) and that the black wires are in the positive position (facing the outside)!<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1086&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1087&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22161b96ce2\" name=\"6a22161b96ce2\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Operate the Trailer Bot<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]This video explains how the Trailer Bot works![\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=Tvr04OzZAKM&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 9 The head [vc_column_text] Attach four short L-frames to one blueboard. When you're finished, flip it upside down. Attach five long L-frames to another blueboard, with the long&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/build-the-trailer-bot\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1736,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":802,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1742,1754,1793,1617,423,626,1533,1438,853,144,59,171],"lesson-tag":[2163,2168,2171,2190,2191],"class_list":["post-1066","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-build","lesson-tag-rokit-smart","lesson-tag-trailer","lesson-tag-trailer-bot","module-trailer","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1066","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":2,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1066\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":1088,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1066\/revisions\/1088"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1736"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1066"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=1066"},{"taxonomy":"les